================================================================================
Modifications
================================================================================

This repository (qinglong-go) is an unofficial Windows port. It is not
affiliated with, endorsed by, or supported by the QingLong project or its
author.

What was changed:

  * The backend was rewritten in Go (originally Node.js/TypeScript under
    back/, static/build/). The HTTP API, authentication scheme, database
    schema and task execution semantics were reproduced from the original
    source so that existing data directories keep working.
  * The front-end build (web/, generated from the upstream src/) is used
    unchanged.
  * The gRPC service definition (back/protos/api.proto), the shell hooks
    (shell/preload/) and the sample scripts are used unchanged, with small
    fixes for Windows path handling.
  * The Node.js runtime, Python and Git for Windows are NOT bundled. Users
    install them separately.

What was removed:

  * The Node.js server process, its TypeScript sources and the PM2 process
    manager. The panel is a single executable.

================================================================================
Third-party components
================================================================================

The executable embeds a minimal set of npm packages required by the ql API
(@grpc/grpc-js, @grpc/proto-loader, protobufjs, undici, nodemailer and their
transitive dependencies). Their licenses are MIT and Apache-2.0; the full texts
are in node_modules/<package>/LICENSE.

Go module dependencies and their licenses are listed by `go list -m all`.
